WEBVTT

00:00:12.310 --> 00:00:15.910
Odaiba Soccer Garden.

00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:01.430
Captain!

00:02:03.180 --> 00:02:04.490
I'll stop you!

00:02:05.130 --> 00:02:11.400
At that velocity, the probability of Captain dodging to the right is 86%!

00:02:14.110 --> 00:02:14.980
Just as I calculated!

00:02:17.980 --> 00:02:20.110
But my calculation was perfect...

00:02:21.490 --> 00:02:22.120
Kusaka!

00:02:24.530 --> 00:02:25.750
Good job, Kusaka!

00:02:25.750 --> 00:02:26.120
Go!

00:02:27.710 --> 00:02:32.130
Real strength means facing what it is that you are afraid of.

00:02:33.380 --> 00:02:40.310
If she hadn't told me what that was, I never would have realized on my own what it is that I was really afraid of.

00:02:42.080 --> 00:02:44.110
<i>I can tell...</i>

00:02:44.110 --> 00:02:46.100
<i>Kusaka-kun is scared...</i>

00:02:46.690 --> 00:02:48.060
<i>Scared?</i>

00:02:48.310 --> 00:02:50.660
<i>What would I be scared of?</i>

00:02:52.150 --> 00:02:54.570
She understood me.

00:02:54.730 --> 00:02:57.610
I want to understand her too, as she has done for me.

00:03:04.290 --> 00:03:06.290
Just you wait, Yuuta! Shun!

00:03:06.550 --> 00:03:09.160
I'll score points in the next game, too!

00:03:10.780 --> 00:03:11.620
It's mine!

00:03:13.440 --> 00:03:13.920
Captain!

00:03:14.290 --> 00:03:15.150
Okay!

00:03:15.640 --> 00:03:16.590
Nice, Matatagi!

00:03:19.310 --> 00:03:21.890
They all keep improving by the minute.

00:03:21.890 --> 00:03:24.060
They're even able to coordinate with each other now.

00:03:25.730 --> 00:03:30.600
If only Mizukawa-san didn't stick by Coach's side all the time and stayed with us. I'm sure she would find that much more fun...

00:03:31.460 --> 00:03:32.350
Kusaka!

00:03:34.780 --> 00:03:35.270
Morimura!

00:03:44.330 --> 00:03:45.400
Not again...

00:03:52.780 --> 00:03:56.440
Matatagi Hayato and Nozaki Sakura.

00:03:56.730 --> 00:04:00.260
And now, Kusaka Ryuuji.

00:04:01.730 --> 00:04:05.000
You predicted that this would happen.

00:04:05.890 --> 00:04:09.060
That's what makes you so confident.

00:04:10.200 --> 00:04:14.950
The real depths of their power have not even been touched upon yet.

00:04:14.950 --> 00:04:17.400
Well, well.

00:04:21.280 --> 00:04:22.150
Tsurugi!

00:04:24.110 --> 00:04:24.980
Minaho!

00:04:26.490 --> 00:04:27.530
Let him shoot!

00:04:27.930 --> 00:04:28.820
I'll stop it!

00:04:29.060 --> 00:04:30.240
Come on, shoot at me!

00:04:36.090 --> 00:04:36.880
Ibuki-kun!

00:04:38.310 --> 00:04:39.670
Damn it...

00:04:41.090 --> 00:04:42.930
Why can't I block it?

00:04:43.840 --> 00:04:44.630
Damn it!

00:04:47.800 --> 00:04:50.730
Okay! That's the end of today's practice.

00:04:50.730 --> 00:04:52.390
Phew, it's over.

00:04:52.970 --> 00:04:54.170
Everyone!

00:04:54.170 --> 00:04:57.400
I have your drinks here, so be sure to rehydrate yourselves!

00:04:57.750 --> 00:04:58.460
Thanks.

00:04:58.460 --> 00:04:59.800
I'm thirsty...

00:04:59.330 --> 00:05:01.900
I think we have a good thing going here.

00:05:02.460 --> 00:05:05.820
We've even increased our momentum by 27%.

00:05:07.380 --> 00:05:11.240
It sure feels great moving my body around!

00:05:11.240 --> 00:05:12.150
Tetsukado.

00:05:14.220 --> 00:05:16.820
Your movements have gotten much sharper.

00:05:16.820 --> 00:05:18.910
But you're able to do better.

00:05:18.910 --> 00:05:20.730
Your speed is dropping.

00:05:20.730 --> 00:05:21.950
Move up more to the front.

00:05:21.950 --> 00:05:23.210
O-Okay...

00:05:28.110 --> 00:05:30.710
Shindou-senpai gave advice...

00:05:30.710 --> 00:05:31.660
Tenma!

00:05:31.660 --> 00:05:32.660
Yeah!

00:05:33.420 --> 00:05:34.560
Shindou-san...

00:05:43.620 --> 00:05:45.020
Here, your drink.

00:05:45.020 --> 00:05:47.240
You need to drink up too, Kusaka-kun.

00:05:47.510 --> 00:05:51.170
You've sweat quite a lot during practice.

00:05:51.170 --> 00:05:53.370
O-Oh, thanks.

00:05:59.440 --> 00:06:02.710
This condo has a supermarket on its first floor!

00:06:02.710 --> 00:06:05.130
And right across the street is a large park!

00:06:07.150 --> 00:06:11.890
In a place like this, no one will be watching over me and I'll get to live the way I want.

00:06:17.530 --> 00:06:19.060
A life of freedom!

00:06:19.060 --> 00:06:20.690
I can't wait!

00:06:20.690 --> 00:06:21.910
Jin-chan!

00:06:24.260 --> 00:06:26.550
Mama... Papa...

00:06:40.710 --> 00:06:44.340
That's... Manabe-kun's parents, huh?

00:06:46.200 --> 00:06:48.220
Jin-chan, wait!

00:06:48.750 --> 00:06:55.850
Your father and I were really surprised when we came back from our overseas business trips and couldn't find you at home...

00:06:56.180 --> 00:06:57.850
Just what are you thinking?

00:06:58.350 --> 00:07:02.780
If you concentrate too much on sports, you'll fall behind in your studies! Your studies are more important!

00:07:02.780 --> 00:07:04.360
I know that, Mama.

00:07:05.110 --> 00:07:08.660
But I'm on the team representing Japan.

00:07:08.660 --> 00:07:13.350
No one could possibly look down on me for having a background in playing for this team.

00:07:13.350 --> 00:07:15.490
Perhaps, but...

00:07:16.130 --> 00:07:18.080
Please, just let me stay here a little longer!

00:07:18.640 --> 00:07:20.860
But what about your studies?

00:07:20.860 --> 00:07:23.080
What good is there in ball-playing?

00:07:23.980 --> 00:07:27.290
I don't understand those willing to involve themselves in such a time waster.

00:07:28.750 --> 00:07:31.420
But there's no point in quarreling over what you've begun.

00:07:31.820 --> 00:07:34.550
I doubt the circumstances allow you to leave right away anyway.

00:07:34.550 --> 00:07:37.290
Withdraw at the appropriate moment and come back home.

00:07:39.580 --> 00:07:41.350
Okay, Papa...

00:07:41.350 --> 00:07:42.980
That is all I have to say.

00:07:44.240 --> 00:07:46.750
Jin-chan, come back soon, you hear?

00:08:04.710 --> 00:08:05.710
Hey there.

00:08:05.710 --> 00:08:07.020
Minaho-kun.

00:08:07.550 --> 00:08:10.640
Sorry, but can you go away?

00:08:10.880 --> 00:08:12.800
You distract me by being here.

00:08:14.110 --> 00:08:16.550
Manabe-kun, are you going to quit soccer?

00:08:18.380 --> 00:08:20.000
You were listening?

00:08:22.350 --> 00:08:25.600
Manabe-kun, why did you join this team?

00:08:25.860 --> 00:08:30.550
Does your reason for participating have something to do with your parents?

00:08:31.240 --> 00:08:33.150
I knew it.

00:08:33.150 --> 00:08:34.950
I thought that was the case.

00:08:36.220 --> 00:08:42.080
In exchange for joining the team, I want to be given the legal right to live independently, away from my parents' reach.

00:08:42.510 --> 00:08:44.540
Huh? Away from your parents?

00:08:45.400 --> 00:08:48.260
You saw them for yourself, so you ought to understand.

00:08:48.260 --> 00:08:53.380
Papa is the head of a top-tier trading company who travels all over the world, and Mama is a diplomat.

00:08:53.380 --> 00:08:55.800
In other words, they're both of the elite class.

00:08:56.460 --> 00:08:59.890
I grew up under their watchful eyes my entire life.

00:08:59.890 --> 00:09:04.290
All they want me to do is study and act as the perfect honor student.

00:09:04.860 --> 00:09:10.520
When I was in elementary, I even stayed behind in cram school and took on extra lessons I didn't need, because I didn't want to go home.

00:09:11.530 --> 00:09:17.000
Parents only think about pushing their values on their children and trying to control them.

00:09:17.000 --> 00:09:18.860
I don't think so.

00:09:18.860 --> 00:09:21.740
At least, it's different with my dad.

00:09:22.180 --> 00:09:25.000
My father is a detective in the police department.

00:09:25.660 --> 00:09:26.620
Detective?

00:09:26.620 --> 00:09:27.000
Yeah.

00:09:27.780 --> 00:09:32.420
He has superior insight and catches even the smallest of details.

00:09:32.420 --> 00:09:37.310
He's known as the Japanese Sherlock Holmes, and he taught me many things.

00:09:37.310 --> 00:09:38.820
He's a wonderful father.

00:09:39.060 --> 00:09:42.380
My dream is to become a detective just like him.

00:09:42.780 --> 00:09:50.460
Even my conditions for this team, that Coach Kuroiwa promised me, is that I get to tour through London's Scotland Yard.

00:09:50.460 --> 00:09:52.440
Hmph, so what?

00:09:52.440 --> 00:09:53.730
Are you making fun of me?

00:09:55.420 --> 00:09:59.240
What you want to say is that your family is a good family, unlike mine, right?

00:09:59.950 --> 00:10:01.690
Sorry, but I'm leaving.

00:10:01.690 --> 00:10:04.260
Ah, no, that's not what I-

00:10:09.920 --> 00:10:12.910
Inazuma Eleven GO Galaxy!

00:10:15.350 --> 00:10:18.200
Inazuma Eleven GO Galaxy!

00:10:24.060 --> 00:10:24.890
This is so good!

00:10:25.420 --> 00:10:27.400
What kind of fish is this?

00:10:27.400 --> 00:10:28.390
It's fat greenling.

00:10:28.910 --> 00:10:29.980
Fat greenling?

00:10:29.980 --> 00:10:31.860
You don't even know what fat greenling is?

00:10:32.480 --> 00:10:39.800
Fat greenling is a white fish that's about this big, and it's called <i>fat</i>  greenling because it has a lot of body fat.

00:10:39.800 --> 00:10:41.980
Tetsukado-kun, you know so much about it!

00:10:41.980 --> 00:10:43.420
Of course I do.

00:10:43.420 --> 00:10:44.950
I come from a family of fishermen.

00:10:44.950 --> 00:10:46.870
Oh, that's right.

00:10:49.750 --> 00:10:50.750
Good morning.

00:10:52.820 --> 00:10:56.090
What? Are you still mad about yesterday?

00:10:56.840 --> 00:11:01.400
You're such a child, being hung up over something so silly.

00:11:01.400 --> 00:11:04.530
You say that you want to live away from your parents,

00:11:04.530 --> 00:11:07.530
but I bet you just want their attention, don't you?

00:11:10.460 --> 00:11:11.730
What was that for?

00:11:11.730 --> 00:11:14.350
What would you know about me, Minaho-kun?

00:11:14.350 --> 00:11:17.290
Don't say random things when you don't even know what I've been through!

00:11:17.290 --> 00:11:19.000
C'mon, fighting first thing in the morning?

00:11:19.000 --> 00:11:20.580
Stop it, you two.

00:11:20.580 --> 00:11:22.420
But Minaho-kun is-

00:11:31.460 --> 00:11:32.460
Can I sit here?

00:11:40.130 --> 00:11:43.200
The semifinals for the Asia district prelims is next.

00:11:43.200 --> 00:11:46.600
You have all done well for these past three matches.

00:11:46.820 --> 00:11:48.930
Really, a lot better than I had expected.

00:11:51.130 --> 00:11:55.730
But at your current level, you cannot possibly win the preliminaries.

00:11:57.080 --> 00:11:59.440
Eager to shoot us right back down, aren't you.

00:11:59.440 --> 00:12:00.710
Follow me.

00:12:14.510 --> 00:12:18.090
I didn't know we had a place like this in the boardinghouse.

00:12:24.290 --> 00:12:25.050
Enter.

00:12:26.290 --> 00:12:27.550
What is this place?

00:12:33.820 --> 00:12:35.330
What a strange room.

00:12:35.330 --> 00:12:35.810
Yeah...

00:12:37.950 --> 00:12:39.320
Is this made out of strengthened glass?

00:12:44.290 --> 00:12:45.440
A meadow?

00:12:45.440 --> 00:12:46.980
What's going on?

00:12:47.910 --> 00:12:49.410
Were we teleported here?

00:12:50.910 --> 00:12:52.060
Matsukaze.

00:12:53.260 --> 00:12:54.540
Run towards me.

00:12:56.820 --> 00:12:57.380
Yes, sir!

00:13:04.970 --> 00:13:05.880
Coach!

00:13:06.200 --> 00:13:07.660
What's going on?

00:13:07.660 --> 00:13:08.890
I can't get closer!

00:13:09.260 --> 00:13:10.890
T-Tenma?

00:13:14.330 --> 00:13:15.420
This is a hologram.

00:13:15.750 --> 00:13:16.900
Hologram?

00:13:17.330 --> 00:13:19.610
But it does not consist of only images.

00:13:20.260 --> 00:13:26.780
By sending signals to your brain, it reproduces the same sensations of the real thing.

00:13:26.780 --> 00:13:28.110
The same sensations?

00:13:32.910 --> 00:13:34.180
Wow!

00:13:34.180 --> 00:13:36.840
This hologram can do so much...

00:13:38.950 --> 00:13:45.420
Beginning today, you will be training in this Black Room which I have devised.

00:13:49.020 --> 00:13:51.260
Now we're in the city?

00:13:51.770 --> 00:13:55.660
For this practice, you must keep the ball as you make decisions based on your surroundings.

00:13:56.950 --> 00:14:00.810
Bring the ball to the other side while avoiding the steel frames.

00:14:01.710 --> 00:14:02.440
Steel frames?

00:14:07.290 --> 00:14:10.400
Of course, your safety is secure.

00:14:10.400 --> 00:14:12.530
Well? Why are you still standing around?

00:14:14.040 --> 00:14:15.370
I'll do it!

00:14:15.800 --> 00:14:16.930
Captain!

00:14:16.930 --> 00:14:21.130
Coach said that we won't win at our current level, right?

00:14:21.130 --> 00:14:22.750
I want to win!

00:14:22.750 --> 00:14:25.260
I want to win the Asia district prelims and go to the world.

00:14:27.660 --> 00:14:28.470
Please begin!

00:14:29.240 --> 00:14:30.930
Then we will start off with Level 1.

00:14:36.020 --> 00:14:36.560
Tenma!

00:14:41.200 --> 00:14:42.640
That was a close one...

00:14:44.240 --> 00:14:45.310
Captain...

00:14:45.840 --> 00:14:47.490
We're going, too!

00:14:49.060 --> 00:14:50.710
Konoha, let's go!

00:14:51.000 --> 00:14:52.490
O-Okay...

00:14:53.460 --> 00:14:54.660
Let's go, too.

00:14:54.660 --> 00:14:55.600
Yes.

00:14:58.550 --> 00:15:00.310
What are you going to do, Manabe-kun?

00:15:00.780 --> 00:15:02.730
Don't look at me...

00:15:04.090 --> 00:15:07.620
I want you two to strengthen your legs.

00:15:07.620 --> 00:15:08.670
Legs?

00:15:13.460 --> 00:15:15.330
This is... a suspension bridge?

00:15:19.620 --> 00:15:21.810
W-We're gonna fall!

00:15:28.350 --> 00:15:29.820
We're saved...

00:15:33.660 --> 00:15:34.570
It repaired itself.

00:15:37.750 --> 00:15:38.830
Now it's coming from this way!

00:15:44.220 --> 00:15:45.820
Do you have one for goalkeepers?

00:15:45.820 --> 00:15:47.580
Yes, of course.

00:15:50.950 --> 00:15:51.760
A desert?

00:15:53.350 --> 00:15:54.820
It's hard to walk around in...

00:15:57.910 --> 00:16:00.240
I see, so that's how it is.

00:16:00.240 --> 00:16:00.730
Come on!

00:16:07.000 --> 00:16:07.730
One more time!

00:16:17.600 --> 00:16:18.440
Is something wrong?

00:16:18.440 --> 00:16:20.410
N-No, nothing!

00:17:06.820 --> 00:17:09.890
Which of you geniuses chose this program?!

00:17:17.350 --> 00:17:19.010
All right, let's go with Level 2.

00:17:20.290 --> 00:17:21.890
It's 1.5 times more the power.

00:17:21.890 --> 00:17:23.800
That's impossible.

00:17:24.240 --> 00:17:26.060
It's because it's impossible that we gotta do it.

00:17:33.930 --> 00:17:35.360
Yeah, let's just stick with Level 1.

00:18:04.930 --> 00:18:06.240
It's over!

00:18:06.240 --> 00:18:12.130
Don't you find it rather strange that he would make amazing facilities like that just for soccer?

00:18:12.130 --> 00:18:16.150
I estimate the expenses it took to make them to be at least several hundred million.

00:18:16.150 --> 00:18:18.200
Definitely not a normal sum of money.

00:18:18.200 --> 00:18:19.660
Well, there's no harm.

00:18:19.660 --> 00:18:23.950
I <i>do</i>  wonder why he would go so far, but we've gotten more powerful because of it.

00:18:24.880 --> 00:18:28.410
Maybe we might even win the championship!

00:18:29.580 --> 00:18:30.330
The championship?

00:18:32.060 --> 00:18:33.930
H-Hold on!

00:18:34.290 --> 00:18:37.400
Are you all really thinking about doing this up to the championship?

00:18:37.400 --> 00:18:38.380
What do you mean?

00:18:39.040 --> 00:18:43.100
Because, there was nothing about winning the championship in our contract.

00:18:44.420 --> 00:18:47.020
Now that you mention it, you have a point.

00:18:47.380 --> 00:18:49.930
The only condition for us is that we participate.

00:18:50.890 --> 00:18:54.200
The contract mentions nothing about the championship.

00:18:54.200 --> 00:18:58.700
Which means, if we quit now, we would still be fulfilling our contract...

00:18:58.950 --> 00:19:00.400
Should I go confirm that?

00:19:00.400 --> 00:19:02.600
No, there's no need.

00:19:02.600 --> 00:19:05.160
Even if I'm not obligated to, I'm staying.

00:19:08.290 --> 00:19:12.730
I want to try facing the fierce emotions that are inside of me.

00:19:13.200 --> 00:19:15.630
And right now, I think that's soccer.

00:19:16.290 --> 00:19:17.730
Fierce emotions...

00:19:18.090 --> 00:19:19.330
Yeah...

00:19:19.330 --> 00:19:20.130
Maybe you're right!

00:19:21.240 --> 00:19:22.800
What about you guys?

00:19:23.180 --> 00:19:26.060
If you all want to stay, then I will too.

00:19:26.660 --> 00:19:28.020
Me too, I guess.

00:19:28.350 --> 00:19:30.180
Ibuki, and you?

00:19:30.440 --> 00:19:32.510
I'm staying, of course.

00:19:32.510 --> 00:19:34.520
I don't accept the way I currently am right now.

00:19:34.800 --> 00:19:37.040
I don't understand.

00:19:37.040 --> 00:19:42.730
What's most important here is getting what we want from our contract, not win the championship.

00:19:45.530 --> 00:19:47.040
What about you, Konoha?

00:19:49.490 --> 00:19:50.840
I...

00:19:51.510 --> 00:19:53.750
Come on, speak more clearly!

00:19:54.380 --> 00:19:56.730
I-I'm sorry...

00:19:59.930 --> 00:20:01.170
Morimu-

00:20:00.310 --> 00:20:01.170
Everyone!

00:20:02.460 --> 00:20:04.910
Your opponent has been decided for the semifinals!

00:20:04.910 --> 00:20:06.850
It's Thailand's team, Mach Tiger.

00:20:07.710 --> 00:20:10.980
They made a complete victory over Qatar's Desert Lion at 5-0!

00:20:23.150 --> 00:20:25.060
5-0?

00:20:25.380 --> 00:20:28.550
But Desert Lion isn't a weak team.

00:20:28.550 --> 00:20:29.480
Yes.

00:20:29.480 --> 00:20:34.000
In fact, in the pre-game evaluation, Desert Lion had a definite overwhelming advantage.

00:20:34.530 --> 00:20:37.670
Come to think of it, there are a lot of upsets in this tournament.

00:20:38.600 --> 00:20:42.690
Many teams that aren't supposed to be particularly strong have been moving up.

00:20:42.690 --> 00:20:44.550
You just realized that?

00:20:45.260 --> 00:20:49.260
In any event, it appears that we're a little ahead of ourselves in thinking we could win the championship.

00:20:51.860 --> 00:20:53.140
They're still quarreling.

00:20:54.090 --> 00:20:56.220
It's idiotic to be upset over someone.

00:20:56.220 --> 00:20:59.040
It's impossible for people to truly understand one another.

00:20:59.040 --> 00:21:02.030
You would be better off just making yourself look like you're getting along with them.

00:21:03.780 --> 00:21:06.740
But since we've already come this far, let's aim for the championship.

00:21:11.000 --> 00:21:12.550
Mach Tiger...

00:21:12.830 --> 00:21:14.080
We won't lose!

00:22:52.850 --> 00:23:07.860
Next Episode

00:22:54.400 --> 00:22:58.020
As we continue to win, Konoha leaves the team.

00:22:58.020 --> 00:23:00.900
This is bad! Let's all go and look for her, guys!

00:23:01.130 --> 00:23:02.650
Next, Self-Hatred.

00:23:02.980 --> 00:23:05.130
This is super-dimensional soccer!

00:23:05.360 --> 00:23:07.860
<b>Self-Hatred</b>

00:23:15.130 --> 00:23:19.600
The Inazuma Eleven GO Galaxy's proverb today is...

00:23:23.460 --> 00:23:25.130
It's because it's impossible that we gotta do it!

00:23:25.530 --> 00:23:26.490
That's all!
